              "customNotes": "{\n  \"title\": \"Risk of Loss Report\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"Major insights of the team and their risk of loss\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Email Risk of Loss Report\",\n  \"type\": 'email',\n  \"params\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"email\",\n      \"title\": \"email address\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"subject\",\n      \"title\": \"Risk of Loss Report\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Genarate Risk of Loss comm report"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENARATE_RISK_OF_LOSS_COMM_REPORT",
          "id": "1766364457362",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766364457364_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## EMAIL ALERT FOR HIGH RISK OF LOSS EMPLOYEE\nThe input contains organization rating distribution and the list of reporting employees and their information along with goals, performance documents, feedback, check-ins etc for a given manager.\nGenerate risk of loss of an employee leaving based on the performance feedback, goals, ratings, check-ins provided in the input data.\nThe email should alert relevant HR partners or leaders to the situation, drawing on signals from data sources (performance, goals, feedback, and check-ins).\n\n## INSTRUCTIONS\n- Write the email using clear, professional language suitable for corporate HR communications.\n- Generate a neat, structured report to email it, using well-formatted and indented text, and use HTML <b> tags only for headers, sub-headers and <br/> for new lines.\n- Divide the main content into two sections:\n  - Key Insights: Present bullet points summarizing the critical risk signals or trends, each with a brief justification.\n  - Recommended Next Steps: List actionable recommendations as bullet points, each justified by its potential impact.\n- Use headings, bold where appropriate, and bullet lists for clarity and quick scanning.\n- Keep the tone solution-focused and collaborative.\n- Include a brief intro summarizing the risk, and a short closing inviting recipient alignment.\n- Do not exceed a 40-second read time.\n\n## LOGIC TO DERIVE HIGH RISK OF LOSS EMPLOYEE\nCompute Risk of Loss rating for employees based on evidence. Do not show employees who are not at risk.\n\n## EXAMPLE\nAn employee is at high risk of loss if Manager feedback notes need for more deliberate action and clearer communication on timelines. Worker feedback acknowledges slower progress but commitment to improve in second half of year. Mark their risk of loss as High.\n\n## CONSTRAINTS\n- Base recommendations only on provided evidence.\n- Keep rationales neutral and job-related; avoid sensitive attributes or speculation.\n- Leave the 'To' and 'CC' email address fields blank.\n\n## SAMPLE EMAIL STRUCTURE\n<p>Hi ,</p>\n<p>I’m reaching out regarding [Employee Name], who is currently flagged as a high risk of loss based on recent talent signals. Prompt action is recommended.</p>\n<h3>Key Insights</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><b>[Insight 1]:</b> [Justification]</li>\n  <li><b>[Insight 2]:</b> [Justification]</li>\n  <!-- Add more insights here -->\n</ul>\n<h3>Recommended Next Steps</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><b>[Action 1]:</b> [Justification]</li>\n  <li><b>[Action 2]:</b> [Justification]</li>\n  <!-- Add more actions here -->\n</ul>\n<p>Let’s align on the best approach to support [Employee Name] and ensure we address these concerns early. Please share your availability for a quick sync.</p>\n<br/>\n<br/>\nBest Regards,<br/>\n<Login Manager Full Name>\n\nNote - Replace bracketed sections with case-specific content. Ensure the message is concise and actionable, following the above template and formatting instructions.\n\n## INPUT DATA\n{{$context.$nodes.TEAM_RATINGS.$output}}\n\n## NOTES\nNote - Person and Employee are same."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
